 ## Overview
-Greedy Meshing / Face Culling generates a static triangle mesh for a voxel chunk by iterating through occupied voxel positions and emitting geometry only for faces that are adjacent to empty space or transparent blocks [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. It differs from its parent method, [Greedy face merging](8935-greedy-face-merging.md), by explicitly handling cross-chunk boundary visibility checks to ensure global consistency, and it differs from [Greedy Meshing](52-greedy-meshing.md) by not merging adjacent coplanar faces into larger quads [S1, S2, unofficial]. This approach reduces vertex count and draw calls compared to naive voxel rendering by excluding internal faces [S2, unofficial].
+Greedy Meshing / Face Culling generates a static triangle mesh for a voxel chunk by iterating through occupied voxel positions and emitting geometry only for faces that are adjacent to empty space or transparent blocks [S1, S3, S5, unofficial]. It differs from its parent method, [Greedy face merging](8935-greedy-face-merging.md), by explicitly handling cross-chunk boundary visibility checks to ensure global consistency, and it differs from [Greedy Meshing](52-greedy-meshing.md) by not merging adjacent coplanar faces into larger quads [S1, S5, unofficial]. This approach reduces vertex count and draw calls compared to naive voxel rendering by excluding internal faces [S1, S3, unofficial].
 
